{#
  _missed_jobs -- "Jobs we did not get", one row per job, with the reference
  that finds it in Towbook. Included by daily_full / weekly_full / monthly_full
  so all three reports say the same thing the same way.

  WHY IT LEADS WITH A REFERENCE. Every other table in these reports is an
  aggregate, and an aggregate cannot answer "why did we not take that one".
  Answering that means opening the offer in Towbook, and that needs the number
  Towbook searches on.

  There are two such numbers and they are NOT interchangeable:

    Job #125169     the Towbook job / call number, searched in Dispatching.
                    Only exists once an offer became a job -- which on this
                    list is the minority, because Towbook does not issue one
                    for an offer nobody accepted.
    Req 324417205   the Digital Request id, found in the Request Log. Present
                    on every offer ever made, so it is what references the
                    ones we turned down or never answered.

  `towbook_ref_label` carries the right one already prefixed; `towbook_ref_kind`
  says which it is. Neither is ever blank -- that is the point of the fallback.

  Context: missed_jobs (list) and missed_jobs_meta (dict), from
  agents/notifier.py -> missed_work_context.
#}
{% if missed_jobs %}
<h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:0 0 4px 0;">Jobs we did not get &mdash; Towbook reference</h3>
<div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;margin-bottom:8px;">
  Every job below is one we were offered and did not run. Quote the reference in
  Towbook to pull the offer up.
  {% if missed_jobs_meta %}
    <strong>{{ missed_jobs_meta.with_job_number | num }}</strong> of
    {{ missed_jobs_meta.shown | num }} carry a Towbook job number;
    the rest never became a job, so they are referenced by their request id.
  {% endif %}
</div>
<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
       style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin-bottom:8px;font-size:13px;">
  <tr style="background:#f0f1f3;">
    <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Towbook ref</th>
    <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Offered</th>
    <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Client</th>
    <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Service</th>
    <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">What happened</th>
    <th align="left" style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;">Reason</th>
  </tr>
  {% for row in missed_jobs or [] %}
  <tr>
    <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;white-space:nowrap;
               font-family:Consolas,Menlo,monospace;
               {% if row.towbook_ref_kind == 'job' %}font-weight:600;color:#1c1c1c;{% else %}color:#555;{% endif %}">
      {{ row.towbook_ref_label or row.towbook_ref }}
    </td>
    <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;white-space:nowrap;color:#444;">
      {{ row.offered_display or row.offered_at_local }}
    </td>
    <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">{{ row.client }}</td>
    <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;color:#444;">{{ row.service_type_raw }}</td>
    <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
      {# The VERBATIM portal status. "Another Provider Responded" and "Expired"
         are the same canonical status and completely different explanations. #}
      {{ row.status_raw or row.status }}
      {% if row.cause and row.cause != 'none' %}<div style="color:#666;font-size:11px;">{{ row.cause }}</div>{% endif %}
    </td>
    <td style="padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;color:#444;">
      {{ row.denial_reason or '&mdash;' | safe }}
    </td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
<div style="color:#888;font-size:11px;margin-bottom:20px;">
  {% if missed_jobs_meta and missed_jobs_meta.truncated %}
    Showing {{ missed_jobs_meta.shown | num }} of
    {{ missed_jobs_meta.missed_in_window | num }} jobs; the dashboard lists them all.
  {% endif %}
  {% if missed_jobs_meta and missed_jobs_meta.job_number_note %}
    {{ missed_jobs_meta.job_number_note }}
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endif %}
